      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limit:\n- **2,550 mg/day:** 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.\n- **Lower dose:** 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day), or 500 mg twice daily if you're starting or titrating.\n- **Single 1,700 mg dose:** I can enter 1,700 mg once or twice daily, which stays under the maximum (3,400 mg/day at twice daily would still exceed it, so once daily is the only option at that dose). Per-dose amounts that large aren't typical, though.\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me the intended dose if 1,700 mg was a typo (for example, 850 mg). I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
